From: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa2-lite: initialize the v2.6L system header table

SDM660 IPA v2.6L keeps the modem header partition in local SRAM, but the
AP header table lives in system memory.  The global ROUTE register selects
that system table.  The lite driver only issued HDR_LOCAL_INIT for v2.6L,
leaving the system table base at zero.  Once AP DMA translation made the TX
descriptor readable, the first routed packet consequently faulted SID 19c0
at IOVA zero and crashed the modem in ipa_hal.c.

Match the downstream v2.6L layout: retain the local modem-header
initialization and additionally allocate the 2048-byte AP DDR header table
and issue HDR_SYSTEM_INIT.  Zero it so offset zero is the two-byte empty
exception header used by the default route.

Also make the no-interrupt TX reaper tolerate a BAM reset racing modem SSR.
Such a reset can move the hardware read pointer past an already-cleared skb
slot; dereferencing that slot caused the secondary ipa_reap_tx NULL Oops.

Signed-off-by: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c b/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
index a6d9308..d1a31fe 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
@@ -1165,6 +1165,16 @@ static int ipa_init_sram_part(struct ipa *ipa, enum ipa_part_id mem_id)
 		 * This is the sequence used by the SDM660 downstream driver.
 		 */
 		if (ipa->version == 26) {
+			ret = devm_ipa_dma_alloc(ipa, &ipa->system_hdr, 2048);
+			if (ret)
+				goto free_pld;
+
+			memset(ipa->system_hdr.virt, 0, ipa->system_hdr.size);
+			cmd->hdr_system_init.hdr_table_addr =
+				ipa->system_hdr.addr;
+			ipa_setup_cmd_desc(desc++, IPA_CMD_HDR_SYSTEM_INIT,
+					   &cmd_args, cmd++);
+
 			cmd->hdr_local_init.hdr_table_src_addr = pld.addr;
 			cmd->hdr_local_init.hdr_table_dst_addr = part_offset;
 			cmd->hdr_local_init.size_hdr_table = part->size;
@@ -1409,10 +1419,17 @@ static int ipa_reap_tx(struct ipa_ep *ep, struct net_device *ndev, int budget)
 	while (done < budget && ep->head != off) {
 		skb = ep->skbs[ep->head];
 		desc = ep->fifo[ep->head];
+		if (WARN_ON_ONCE(!skb)) {
+			dev_err(dev,
+				"TX completion without skb: pipe=%u head=%u hw=%u\n",
+				ep->id, ep->head, off);
+			break;
+		}
 
 		bytes += skb->len;
 		packets++;
 
+		ep->skbs[ep->head] = NULL;
 		dma_unmap_single(dev, desc.addr, skb->len, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
 		dev_consume_skb_any(skb);
 		atomic_inc(&ep->free_descs);
